Imagine owning a house on Butler Street. The neighborhood has about 100 homeowners on Butler Street and South Street, about 50 per street, with similar incomes. Property prices have fallen 25% and the area is becoming less desirable. You are not very concerned now, but a sale in a few years could bring even less. A £500 property-tax discount must be spent improving the house, street or neighborhood. You may improve your own house, contribute to your street committee fund, or to the joint neighborhood fund. South Street has its own separate street fund. Property values have declined further during the last month. Your street enters Best Street in the Neighborhood, competing against South Street;winning benefits your street properties. Imagine being highly motivated to win the cash prize.
